  <!--
    x64 only. Two independent gating macros split what used to be one
    (EMOT3_DIST):
      EMOT3_DIST     - strips the AV-sensitive input-SWALLOWS (QuickbarWheel,
                       SendSuppress, DevSettings/dev.json). Defined by
                       Distribution + DistributionDevTools. See src/dev/QuickbarWheel.h.
      EMOT3_DEVTOOLS - includes the diagnostic dev TOOLS (perf overlay, QB
                       sizing readout, runtime state inspector). Present only
                       when defined. See src/dev/DevTools.h. (All dev-only code
                       lives in src/dev/, which is on the include path.)

    Five configurations (-> output DLL):
      Debug                - unoptimized, debug CRT, for stepping. Dev tools on,
                             swallows on.                          -> emot3.dll
      Distribution         - optimized, EMOT3_DIST. No swallows, no dev tools.
                             The shipped public build (CI publishes). -> emot3.dll
      Plus                 - optimized. Swallows on, no dev tools. The
                             convenience build for power users.  -> emot3_plus.dll
      Dev                  - optimized. Swallows on + dev tools on. The local
                             diagnostic build.                    -> emot3_dev.dll
      DistributionDevTools - optimized, EMOT3_DIST + EMOT3_DEVTOOLS. Swallows
                             stripped but dev tools on - diagnose a dist-shaped
                             binary.                       -> emot3_distdevtools.dll
    Each configuration writes to its own folder under build\ (see OutDir/IntDir
    below) so builds never clobber each other and incremental state survives
    config switches. TargetName is per-config so the DLLs don't collide.
  -->
